 "headline": "",
 "intro": "IHC CONCEPTUALIZED 5 ‘CAPTAIN MARVEL’-THEMED STEREOGRAMS THAT WERE SHARED ACROSS MARVEL PROPERTIES AND GARNERED OVER 1 BILLION MEDIA IMPRESSIONS.",
 "introPieces": [
  {
   "type": "text",
   "html": "<p>‍</p>"
  },
  {
   "type": "introGallery",
   "media": [
    {
     "type": "image",
     "src": "/images/66161938653508b168ac9343_helmet-sird01-1800x-min.webp",
     "alt": ""
    },
    {
     "type": "image",
     "src": "/images/66161939fe25de0407ff5524_cap-battleoutfit-1800x-min.webp",
     "alt": ""
    }
   ],
   "html": "<p>For the release of Captain Marvel, Marvel Studios enlisted IHC to create a series of stereograms as a digital stunt. From 1993-1995 the ‘Magic Eye’ craze tore through the globe, these seemingly random digital patterns revealed hidden images if the user stared at them long enough.</p>\n<p>Set in 1995, Captain Marvel takes place at the height of the mania surrounding the puzzles and employs a narrative full of hidden meanings, duplicitous characters, and unassuming clues. A seemingly perfect pairing for an online campaign utilizing 3D stereograms.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "LAUNCH CONTENT",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>We created 5 unique stereograms, each capturing a character in the forthcoming Captain Marvel film. The illusions serve as both a clear promotion for the film’s release as well as a fun reminder of the magic from the time.</p>",
     "right": "<p>Since the technology used to create these images was primarily outdated, IHC needed to work internally to re-make it in a way that captured the original effect while also working on social media.</p>"
    },
